<h2 id="onlyref-when" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">1. When this applies</h2>

| Trigger | Meaning |
|---------|---------|
| User types **`onlyref`** (and usually names an issue domain, e.g. batch verify LM prompt redundancy) | Produce or revise a **numbered-phase refactor plan** **`.md`** only. |

**Companion execution rule:** **`implref`** / **`resumimpl`** on the same plan files — **see** `.cursor/rules/implref-resumimpl-refactor-plan-followthrough.mdc`.

**Canonical exemplar strand (this codebase):** refocus **`vt_p_v3_batch_verify`** / single-unit parity so repair prompts **lead with plain, precise deterministic-failure narration** (see **`checker_feedback_plain_for_verify_context`** and **`build_batch_verify_prompt`**) instead of drowning the LM in mirrored **`scaffold_contract`**, **`repair_hints`**, and duplicate checker blocks — without changing greedy injector semantics in the planning pass.

Evidence helpers when the user cites them (update the plan front-matter references if needed):

| Path |
|------|
| `cursor_gen/COMPARE_unit1_augment_vs_verify_round1.md` |
| `cursor_gen/extracted_batch_augment_unit1_prompt.json` |
| `cursor_gen/extracted_batch_verify_round1_prompt.json` |
| `cursor_gen/llm_prompts_json/unit1_augment_vs_verify_round1_diff.json` |

