<h2 id="onlyref-shape" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">3. Plan shape checklist (<code>[ ]</code> / <code>[X]</code>)</h2>

The output **Markdown MUST** satisfy the same structural bar **implref** expects (see **`implref-resumimpl-refactor-plan-followthrough.mdc`** — document outline **section 2**):

| Requirement | Detail |
|-------------|--------|
| **Phases numbered** | `1. Phase …`, `2. Phase …`; optional `[X]` on phase headings when fully done (**only apply `[X]` if the user later completed work outside `onlyref`—default new plans stay all `[ ]`**). |
| **Checklists** | Every actionable deliverable prefixed **`[ ]`** (new plans) unless recording already-finished legacy work the user enumerated explicitly. |
| **Quality bar subsection** | Tests + informative comments/documentation expectations spelled out (**implref step 2**). |
| **MRKD authoring** | **`.cursor/rules/mrkd-markdown-authoring.mdc`** — numbered document outline near top (after optional HTML **`<h1>`** title); at most **`#`** / **`##`** / **`###`** Markdown depth alongside HTML tinted headings **if** previews matter. Avoid section-symbol glyphs in user-facing headings or body (**use "section", "phase", or "step 3.5-style" wording** instead). |
| **Cross-links** | Link to **`implref`** for execution boundary; cite source modules (`paragraph_bracket_markup.py`, `conjugation_paragraph_batch_generator.py`, `conj_paragraph_prompt_config.py`, YAML paths). |

**Location:** **[Plan folder lifecycle](#onlyref-folders)** — **`cursor_gen/refactor_plans/new/REFACTOR_*.md`** only.

