<h2 id="onlyref-steps" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">4. Authoring procedure</h2>

1. **Infer or ask one narrow question:** If repo path ambiguous, confirm target filename or create **`cursor_gen/refactor_plans/new/REFACTOR_<SHORT_TOPIC>.md`** (MRKD outline + **onlyref** shape).

2. **Read code touchpoints:** At minimum skim **`paragraph_bracket_markup.py`** (`checker_feedback_plain_for_verify_context`, injector codes) and **`conjugation_paragraph_batch_generator.py`** (`build_batch_verify_prompt`). If single-unit parity at risk, note **`conjugation_paragraph_generator.py`**.

3. **Freeze evidence:** Embed a short table referencing **`cursor_gen/*COMPARE*`** / **`extracted_*`** dumps or **`logs/llm_traffic`** bundles when serlog-informed (grep gitignored **`logs/`** per **`.cursor/rules/serlog-search-gitignored-logs.mdc`** when needed).

4. **Write phases** covering: deterministic prose thoroughness (**all error codes ↔ English** strategy), duplication audit (**context keys ranked by redundancy**), feature-flag rollout, parity tests (**batch + single-unit**), reconciliation with prior plans (e.g. **`REFACTOR_PLGW_BATCH_PROMPT_TRIM_*.md`** B.1).

5. **Quality bar:** Explicit bullets for tests (unit + integration snapshots) and **cdcm** comments — file headers; **≥1 doc line per class and per function/method** in touched modules ([cdcm per-symbol](.cursor/rules/cdcm-code-comments.mdc#cdcm-per-symbol)); inline notes where non-obvious — not vague "add comments someday."

6. **Finish with:** **Deferred / follow-ups** table for risky or product-owned items (**OpenAI prompt caching**, pure UI diagnostics, etc.).

