<h2 id="onlyref-forbid" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">5. Hard stops — <code>onlyref</code> must not</h2>

Unless the user explicitly issues a **separate** instruction (**`implref`**, permissive refactor message, bugfix request):

| Forbidden | Reason |
|-----------|--------|
| Implement phases, refactor Python/TS/YAML **`main` behavior**, flip **`[ ]` → `[X]`** pretending work ran | Boundary of **`onlyref`** is **documentation / plan-only**. |
| Run broad refactors touching production paths "because the plan says so later" | That is **`implref`** scope after plan approval. |
| Append **war stories** claiming resolution | Allowed only alongside **completed** **`implref`** phases per **`.cursor/rules/exwar-war-stories-extraction.mdc`**. **`onlyref`** may **mention** candidate story themes **inside** the plan prose only. |

**Allowed edits under `onlyref`:** refactor plan **`*.md`**, optional scratch notes under **`cursor_gen/refactor_notes/`** if user permits scratch artifacts—not application code.

